[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-88f14287-8f56-4384-ac32-ea16d27905fb\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p><strong>Tue 7 Jul 2026 15:10 - 15:30 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/fse-2026/fse-2026-venue-mb-3.270\" class=\"room-link navigate\">MB 3.270</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers#program\" class=\"navigate\">Agents</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/michaelpradel\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Michael Pradel</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"88f14287-8f56-4384-ac32-ea16d27905fb\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Reducing Cost of LLM Agents with Trajectory Reduction</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Multi-turn agent systems based on Large Language Models (LLMs) have been increasingly popular for software engineering tasks. While LLM agents show decent effectiveness, the high computational cost of input tokens due to the ever-growing trajectory remains an efficiency concern for their applications. Efficiency is largely neglected in existing studies and agent products, and this paper fills the gap by introducing an inference-time trajectory reduction approach to reduce the cost of agents.</p>\n<p>Through analyzing existing agent trajectories, we demonstrate that useless, redundant, and expired information is widespread in all trajectories, which can be identified and reduced without harming the agent\u2019s performance. We then design a simple yet effective trajectory reduction approach, AgentDiet, which automatically removes such waste information. We implement AgentDiet on a top-performing coding agent, and the evaluation on two LLMs and two benchmarks shows that AgentDiet can reduce input tokens by 39.9% ~ 59.7%, or the final computational cost by 21.1% ~ 35.9%, while maintaining the same agent performance. This indicates that trajectory reduction is a promising direction for agent systems.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.23586\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> Pre-print</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/yuananxiao\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yuan-An Xiao<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Peking University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/pengfeigao2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Pengfei Gao\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/pengfeigao2/f02b2a8b-ab52-4d5e-8b36-f52875f17a05/micro-avatar?1784966718000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Pengfei Gao<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">ByteDance</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/chaopeng\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Chao Peng\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/chaopeng/e3005471-9003-4a5b-9c90-c00b504188e4/micro-avatar?1784966718000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Chao Peng<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Tencent</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/yingfeixiong\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Yingfei Xiong\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/yingfeixiong/c4005bc7-5083-4173-aa8b-a14c81e4165e/micro-avatar?1791621359000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yingfei Xiong<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Peking University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers/137/Reducing-Cost-of-LLM-Agents-with-Trajectory-Reduction\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-88f14287-8f56-4384-ac32-ea16d27905fb').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
